## 2. PostgreSQL Ingestion: Batch INSERT vs. `pg-copy-streams` (COPY)

### Comparison & Selection Strategy

| Criteria | Multi-Row Parameterized `INSERT` | `pg-copy-streams` (`COPY FROM STDIN`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Speed** | Fast ($\approx 5,000 - 15,000\text{ rows/sec}$) | Ultra Fast ($\approx 30,000 - 80,000\text{ rows/sec}$) |
| **Error Isolation** | **High** (Can catch, retry, or isolate bad rows) | **All-or-Nothing** (Single invalid row fails whole batch) |
| **UPSERT Support** | Supported (`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING / UPDATE`) | Not supported natively |
| **Complexity** | Simple, reliable, easy to debug | Requires CSV/Binary stream formatting |
| **Recommendation** | **Primary choice for academic & standard migrations** | **Recommended for multi-million row massive loads** |

* **Optimal Multi-Row Query Structure:**
  ```sql
  INSERT INTO users (id, name, email, created_at)
  VALUES 
    ($1, $2, $3, $4),
    ($5, $6, $7, $8),
    ...
  ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
  ```

